  - "scientific-machine-learning"
abstract: "AstroMap-AI is an end-to-end scientific platform that ingests photometric light curves from NASA TESS and Kepler archives, employs a dual-domain Physics-Informed Neural Network (PINN-TransNet) with 2D Continuous Wavelet Scalograms and Mandel-Agol analytical transit constraints, and performs automated astrophysical false-positive vetting (Robovetter). Evaluated on a 1,000-target statistical benchmark and real TESS observations from Sector 1, AstroMap-AI achieves 89.7% accuracy, 92.8% recall, 91.5% precision, and 100% orbital period recovery."
